  "details": "I believe it would be beneficial to the avatar development community to increase the number of synced bits for avatars from 256 to 512, 1024, or 2048.\n\nThis change would enable more customizable avatars without too much of a server load deficit, If they are in fact \"bits\" it only adds a tiny amount of transferred data compared to the avatars themselves. \n\nThis would allow avatar creators to be more creative and have more options without clunky/complicated workarounds such as \"OSC Parameter Sync\" (by Fuuujin)\n\nAnother worthy consideration is to allow a higher amount of bits but more than 256 will guarantee a very poor avatar rank (or another similar \"cost\").",
